{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"6192bf8302a20700d883f8e27bea46437d6551e0edf9af2f3e111980a50fd0aa","digest":{"component_or_area":"Operation-scoped configuration and provider-auth composition","key_entities":["OperationSnapshot","RP-04","RP-01","ADR 0098","PydanticAIRunner","ProviderSession","LLMRuntime","GitRuntime","BridgeRuntime","op-cert","REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH","REBAR_OPCERT_PRIVATE_KEY","REBAR_ROOT","REBAR_OPERATION_SNAPSHOT_SHADOW","check_config_reads.py","SecretStr","SecretBytes"],"problem_keywords":["configuration composition","credential handling","authentication","operation scoping","provider lifecycle","environment isolation","secrets management"],"propositions":["Rebar must resolve one immutable, serializable, non-secret OperationSnapshot at each operation boundary using a single precedence order: explicit operation input > environment > project config > user config > schema default.","Configuration and ambient state must not be reread mid-operation; once resolved, OperationSnapshot remains stable across environment/file/cwd mutations until the next operation boundary.","Provider-native authentication (Git, LLM, bridge, MCP, review-bot, op-cert) must be composed consistently at operation/startup boundaries through subsystem-local factories without arbitrary client injection or cross-provider fallback.","Static credentials must use provider-specific Pydantic SecretStr/SecretBytes carriers, revealed only in sending adapters, and never exposed through global os.environ mutation or serialization.","Op-cert must enforce exclusive startup resolution from exactly one of REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH or REBAR_OPCERT_PRIVATE_KEY, validate before service work, store in process-owned 0700/0600 files, and receive no per-job retrieval or runtime SSM coupling.","An AST ownership gate must derive config/credential names from authoritative registries, reject direct/aliased reads below approved seams, enforce exact path/symbol+rationale exceptions, reach zero legacy exceptions at cutover, and detect schema/docs divergence."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787542092412364001,"uuid":"764b2806-ada1-4448-912d-e00d614221dd"}